  "the raw taste line saying no pump can move water without viscosity was not carried; displacement pumps move fluid by geometry",
  "the raw taste line saying fatigue cracks inevitably break a shaft after ten million cycles was not carried; the opposite claim of indefinite life below an endurance limit is not carried either",
  "fact-check: some steels show a practical endurance limit near ten million cycles in air at constant amplitude, but gigacycle failures from subsurface inclusions (Bathias 1999), corrosion, and variable loading mean it guarantees no infinite life",
  "the thermodynamics hub survives as canonical nodes and concept tags, not as its own folder",
  "the exergy pedagogy hypothesis with an invented 50 percent figure was dropped",
